FOG114	1988	FOG-CPM.114	1987	Y	UNARC   .COM	FF9D	5K	1.6	UnARChive utility 1 of 6	 Restores files compacted with the MS-DOS ARChive utilities. Note that, like crunched files, not all versions use the same compression technique and can therefore be incompatible with each other. This version extracts all ARC and ARK files know at the time of the release of this disk. ASseMbler source (SLR or M80) is included in an ARC file.	'Conservation of disk space is of primary interest to all users.' The whole era in one line: every design decision on every disk here was made inside a **182 KB** budget -- the capacity of a double-density Osborne disk, and double what a single-density machine gave you a year earlier.	The sentence that explains the whole library. I want a newcomer to read it and realise that '182 KB' was not a limitation people complained about -- it was the design brief. AND it was double the size it was only a short time ago (if you had the double density upgrade!)
