FOG158	flat	--FOGCPM.158			C128MOD .DOC	57CC				Explaination of new CPM+.SYS that reads Otrona C1571/2 .COM: DB A9 New version speeds up drive access	**Commodore C-128 programs**, on a disk in the *First Osborne* Group library. By the late 1980s FOG had outlived the machine it was named for and become a general CP/M users' group -- and the library's composition over time shows exactly that.	C-128 programs in the *Osborne* library. This is the fact I would put in front of a newcomer first: the group outlived the machine. It makes the whole thing a human story rather than a parts catalogue. And underscores how brutally under appreciated the C128 is. I love my C64 Ultimate, but a C128 Ultimate would be EPIC.
